            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_204N20137">
               <date isodate="1876-01-26" xml:id="date_N20393">1876-01-26</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_204N20135">
               <p xml:id="idm96">Axel Liebmann (1849 -1876) was one of the first students at the Academy of Music in Copenhagen, founded in 1865. 1868 -1871 he was assistant conductor of Studenter-Sangforeningen, and in 1873 he was co-founder of Korforeningen (The Choral Society). In 1874 he was appointed organist at Garnisonskirken, the same church where Hartmann had been organist 1824 -1843. When Hartmann's Symphony No. 2 had its second performance in 1875, it had been revised by Liebmann.</p>
            </history>
